.TH MMAP_READAT 3
.SH NAME
mmap_readat \- map a file relative to a directory file descriptor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "mmap.h"
.PP
.BI "const char* mmap_readat(const char* " filename ", size_t* " filesize ", int " dirfd ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mmap_readat
opens the file
.I filename
relative to the directory file descriptor
.I dirfd
using
.BR openat (2),
then maps the file into memory as a shared, read-only mapping.
The file is closed after the mapping is created.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the mapped memory (or an empty string if the file is empty) on success, or NULL on failure.